# s4-engine-actions-page: `evaluate` keeps the refs of a script that provably left the page alone (the old `settledRevision` before and after, "The script left
# the page unchanged ..."). The old engine compared the document revision itself; the revision is the host's to read, so the host does the comparison and says
# the result. Both fields are optional: an older host answers none and the engine then takes a fresh snapshot after every script (never wrong, only costlier).

